WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.636 line:0%
-Hey, Doc?
-Mm-hmm?

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:08.508 line:0%
-I know it's Thursday,
but I was thinking tonight

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:13.279 line:0%
could be a-a good night
for sex night possibly.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.016 line:0%
-Ooh.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:21.487 line:0%
It's an interesting idea,
but, you know...

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.956 line:0%
Thursdays.

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:25.191
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.960
We're here with Anne Hathaway,
everybody!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.830
That was a clip
from "She Came to Me."

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.065
And you --
Your wonderful co-star,

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.434
Peter Dinklage, he plays --
what would you call it --

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.236
opera composer?
-Yes.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.004
-Yes.
-He plays an opera composer

00:00:39.004 --> 00:00:42.408
who is on year five
of an artistic blockage.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.277
-Gotcha.
And you play a therapist?

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.678
-I was his therapist.
-Okay.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.947
-And then we got married.
-Oh, that's always good.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.883
-They say that you should
definitely do that.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:53.252
-And one day,
I'm feeling a little --

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:56.556
I'm feeling like I need
a little bit of space from him.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.658
And so I send him off on a walk,

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.226
and I tell him
to interact with a stranger,

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.861
and he winds up
meeting Marisa Tomei,

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.362
who's a tugboat captain,

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.498
and she takes him
back to her tugboat

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.100
where she reveals to him
while disrobing

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.137
that she is
a sex and love addict.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.839
-Oh, wow.
-Yes.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.875
-So never tell your spouse
to take a walk.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.910
You never know --
never know what might happen.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.813
-Well, just when you feel
really sorry for my character,

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.115
because she is successful
in seducing him,

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:24.984
you realize that I am

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.086
actually in a secret
relationship with God.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.988
-Oh! Well, there you go!

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.924
It's so what I love
about indie movies.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.258
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.027
Did you enjoy
playing a therapist?

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.862
-I did.
I did enjoy playing a therapist.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.496
I was really nervous
about, like,

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:39.031
you know,
just getting it right

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:40.533
and making sure --
it can be quite serious.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.401
But yeah, yeah, it felt like

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:45.505
I could put a lot of things
I have learned to use.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.873
-Yeah, that would be my fear,
if I ever played a therapist,

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:51.244
is that one of mine would go,
"Is that me?"

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.079
You had a really a cool thing,
which is --

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.948
Again, we mentioned
that you're a producer.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.915
One of the things
you have to do is reach out,

00:01:56.915 --> 00:01:59.085
try to find people
to help you with your movie.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.554
For the soundtrack,
you had somebody write a song.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.457
-Yes, yes, yes. Rebecca was the
one that reached out to him.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.726
But our title song,
the end-credits song,

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.093
is written by Bruce Springsteen.

00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:09.729
-That's really incredible.
-I know!

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.597
-And the day you find out
that he's gonna do it,

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:14.466
it just must be --
What a celebration.

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:16.636
-I mean, it was kind of one of
those moments that was so cool.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.571
You expect, like,
everything to explode,

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.074
but instead it goes quiet.
You know what I mean?

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:25.211
Like, it's so --
it's so impossible to imagine.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:28.514
He's -- Yeah, he's so mythic
in his -- in his way.

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.516
-Yes. And very sage.
When you actually talk to him,

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.285
he seems to have
a very deep wisdom

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.652
that not a lot of people have.

00:02:33.652 --> 00:02:35.955
-Oh. my gosh. I couldn't.
I couldn't talk to him.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.524
I couldn't possibly do it.

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:39.893
-Yeah, the first time I met him,

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:42.662
he did music
my first year on "SNL."

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.029
And I just had to do that thing,

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:46.299
which is I had to just --
I had to say a thing to him

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.434
that he's heard a hundred times
and just walk over and be like,

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.036
"Hey, I just want to say..."

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.105
And he was like, "Cool. How's
the show gonna be this week?"

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.873
And I just like, "Uh..."
And just walked away.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.642
I was like, "Oh, I'm not ready

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.309
to have, like,
a back-and-forth here.

00:02:57.309 --> 00:02:59.045
This isn't a conversation.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.414
This is me unburdening and
running away as fast as I can."

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:04.017
-I just also love the way
you so casually just said,

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.919
"Yeah, Bruce Springsteen
was the musical guest

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.420
the first week
that I was on 'SNL.'"

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.322
Like, you just dropped that
so casually.

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:11.758
Do you ever hear yourself?

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.125
-It was my second season.
He was the first.

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.927
-Oh, it was your second.
Okay. Got it. Got it. Got it.

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.528
-I don't remember
all of the musical guests,

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:18.631
but I remember that,
and I remember The Killers

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.133
'cause they're still on the lam.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.668
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:24.504
You've had time on.
I know you love Broadway.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.472
You are a theater kid,
through and through.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.808
-It's true. It's true.
-Have you managed to see stuff

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.643
during this downtime?
-Oh!

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.546
I saw -- A few months ago now,

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:37.083
but I saw my wonderful friend
Jessica Chastain,

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.351
like, levitate on stage
in "A Doll's House."

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:40.686
Did anybody here get to see it?

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:41.920
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-[ Gasps ]

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.423
It's like nothing
I've ever seen.

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:45.791
She was -- She was -- I mean,
just -- She was everything.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.627
And then it's so cool
that David Byr--

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.762
I mean, for so many reasons
it's so cool that
David Byrne is here,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.464
but I can't wait
to see "Here Lies Love."

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.199
I got to see it at the Public.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:54.767
-During the first run of it.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.836
And so I'm so excited to go see
it, just as soon as we're done.

00:03:57.836 --> 00:03:59.872
-Alright. Well, I am
so happy to have you here.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.741
It's always just such a delight
to see you.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.809
Congratulations on the film.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:06.579
-And we always want you
to come back.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.682
Anne Hathaway. "She Came to Me"
is in theaters October 6th.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:12.051 line:0%
Stick around. We'll be
right back with David Byrne.

